IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poa-dates`
IMPORT `poa-rules`
IMPORT `poa-seat`
IMPORT `poa-seat-attorney`

-- Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) -- worked cases for the questions of the attorney (poa-seat-attorney.l4), and
-- MIRROR CASES: the same facts asked from the principal's seat (poa-seat.l4) and the attorney's, with answers that
-- agree. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative: an
-- injured principal whose adult daughter is attorney for financial matters.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: the attorney, and mirror cases`

`fin` MEANS `a financial matter (including a legal matter about my money or property, such as my injury claim)`
`both` MEANS `both personal and financial matters`
`for both` MEANS `for both personal and financial matters`
`for fin` MEANS `for financial matters only`
`for pers` MEANS `for personal matters only`
`cease` MEANS `when I cease to have decision making capacity for the matter`
`none` MEANS `no exception`
`joint buy` MEANS `acquiring property to be held jointly with my attorney, or a loan or guarantee for it`
`eligible` MEANS `yes: an individual eligible under s 28(1)`

§§ `s 28 -- am I eligible (with mirrors)`

-- Arguments: my age, matters, insolvent, dishonesty, disclosed, paid to care, carer payment, health provider,
-- accommodation provider.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be the attorney` 30 `for both` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `eligible`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be the attorney` 17 `for both` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: under 18 (s 28(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be the attorney` 30 `for fin` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: convicted or found guilty of an offence involving dishonesty, not disclosed to me and recorded in the power (s 28(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be the attorney` 30 `for pers` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `eligible`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be the attorney` 30 `for both` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `eligible`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be the attorney` 30 `for both` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: my care worker, health provider or accommodation provider (s 28(1)(d))`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be the attorney` 30 `for both` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an insolvent under administration (s 28(1)(b))`

-- Mirrors: the daughter, 30, on a carer payment and also paid from the compensation; then the same, not on a carer
-- payment; then with an undisclosed dishonesty conviction, for financial matters.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be the attorney` 30 `for both` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Can this person be my attorney` `an individual` `for both` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be the attorney` 30 `for both` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Can this person be my attorney` `an individual` `for both` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be the attorney` 30 `for fin` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Can this person be my attorney` `an individual` `for fin` 30 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `ss 39, 41, 83 -- may I act now (with mirrors)`

-- Arguments: scope, matter, start, time come, lacks capacity, began acting, administration order, guardianship order,
-- VCAT authorised.
#ASSERT `May I act as attorney now` `both` `fin` `cease` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: while I do not have decision making capacity for the matter (s 39(1)(b), (3))`
#ASSERT `May I act as attorney now` `both` `fin` `cease` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: not yet; the time I specified has not come and I have capacity for the matter (s 39)`
#ASSERT `May I act as attorney now` `both` `fin` `cease` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: VCAT has made an administration or guardianship order covering the matter and has not authorised my attorney (s 83)`
#ASSERT `May I act as attorney now` `both` `fin` `cease` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `May my attorney act for me now` `both` `fin` `cease` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I act as attorney now` `both` `fin` `cease` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `May my attorney act for me now` `both` `fin` `cease` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I act as attorney now` `both` `fin` `cease` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `May my attorney run or settle my claim now` `both` `cease` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE

-- s 40: arguments first time, names people.
#ASSERT `Must I notify anyone before I first act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I notify anyone before I first act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I notify anyone before I first act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Part 6 -- my dealings (with mirrors)`

-- Arguments: financial attorney, conflict, exception, capacity then, principal authorised, VCAT authorised, completed,
-- principal validated, VCAT validated. The daughter uses the damages to buy a unit in both names after the principal
-- lost capacity: a conflict transaction, not excepted (s 64(2)(c)(iii) needs the principal's capacity).
#ASSERT `May I enter into this transaction` TRUE TRUE `joint buy` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a conflict transaction my attorney must not enter into without my or VCAT's authority (s 64(1))`
#ASSERT `May I enter into this transaction` TRUE TRUE `joint buy` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: VCAT authorised it beforehand (s 65(4))`
#ASSERT `May I enter into this transaction` TRUE TRUE `joint buy` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `May my attorney enter into this conflict transaction` TRUE TRUE `joint buy` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I enter into this transaction` TRUE TRUE `joint buy` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `May my attorney enter into this conflict transaction` TRUE TRUE `joint buy` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I enter into this transaction` TRUE TRUE `none` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `May my attorney enter into this conflict transaction` TRUE TRUE `none` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- Arguments: financial attorney, forbidden, reasonable, seasonal, donation.
#ASSERT `May I make this gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I make this gift` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I make this gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `May my attorney make this gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I make this gift` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `May my attorney make this gift` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I make this gift` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `May my attorney make this gift` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- s 67(3): arguments connected, value, prescribed amount (0 = none prescribed).
#ASSERT `Must I keep a written record of this gift` TRUE 100 0 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I keep a written record of this gift` TRUE 99.99 0 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I keep a written record of this gift` FALSE 1000 0 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I keep a written record of this gift` TRUE 150 200 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I keep a written record of this gift` TRUE 200 200 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I keep a written record of this gift` TRUE 50 50 EQUALS TRUE

-- s 66: arguments financial, material.
#ASSERT `Must I keep records of this dealing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I keep records of this dealing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I keep records of this dealing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 68: arguments financial attorney, power provides, reasonable, power allows more.
#ASSERT `May I provide for the principal's dependant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I provide for the principal's dependant` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I provide for the principal's dependant` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I provide for the principal's dependant` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I provide for the principal's dependant` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 69: arguments financial attorney, joint.
#ASSERT `Must I keep my property separate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I keep my property separate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I keep my property separate` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 70 (with mirrors).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be paid` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be paid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be paid` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Is my attorney entitled to be paid` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be paid` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Is my attorney entitled to be paid` FALSE TRUE

-- ss 71, 72 (with mirrors): arguments several, otherwise, depletion.
#ASSERT `What happens if I disagree with the other attorney` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the financial matters attorney must not implement it but must apply to VCAT, as it would seriously deplete my finances (s 72(2))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I disagree with the other attorney` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `What happens when my attorneys disagree` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `What happens if I disagree with the other attorney` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `What happens when my attorneys disagree` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§§ `Ending my role`

-- Arguments: alternative, acting, principal capable, another attorney, alternative willing.
#ASSERT `May I resign now` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: at any time while the principal has capacity for the matter, in the prescribed form, telling the principal and the other attorneys (ss 56-58)`
#ASSERT `May I resign now` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: there is another attorney with power for the matter; in the prescribed form, telling the other attorneys and alternative attorneys (ss 59(1)(a), 60, 61(1))`
#ASSERT `May I resign now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: an alternative attorney with power for the matter is able and willing to act; in the prescribed form, telling the alternative attorneys (ss 59(1)(b), 60, 61(2))`
#ASSERT `May I resign now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only with leave from VCAT or the Supreme Court (s 59(1)(c) or (2))`
#ASSERT `May I resign now` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only with leave from VCAT or the Supreme Court (s 59(1)(c) or (2))`
#ASSERT `May I resign now` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an alternative attorney who is not acting may resign; in the prescribed form, telling the attorneys and other alternative attorneys (ss 59(3), 60, 61(3))`
#ASSERT `May I resign now` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: at any time while the principal has capacity for the matter, in the prescribed form, telling the principal and the other attorneys (ss 56-58)`

-- s 54(3), (4): arguments revoked, principal capable, another attorney, alternative, can reach relative.
#ASSERT `Whom must I notify that my appointment ended` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Whom must I notify that my appointment ended` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `the principal`, `every other attorney`, `every alternative attorney`
#ASSERT `Whom must I notify that my appointment ended` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `the principal`
#ASSERT `Whom must I notify that my appointment ended` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `every other attorney`
#ASSERT `Whom must I notify that my appointment ended` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS LIST `every alternative attorney`
#ASSERT `Whom must I notify that my appointment ended` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS LIST `the principal's nearest relative`
#ASSERT `Whom must I notify that my appointment ended` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `the Public Advocate, if the nearest relative cannot be notified`

§§ `My liability (with mirrors)`

-- Arguments: contravention, court advice, invalid or revoked, good faith, relief, principal died.
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to compensate the principal` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no relief` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court or VCAT may order my attorney to compensate me (s 77(1))`
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to compensate the principal` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `no relief` FALSE EQUALS `no: my attorney acted on the advice, direction or order of the Supreme Court or VCAT and is taken to have complied (ss 76, 77(3))`
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to compensate the principal` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `relieved of part` TRUE EQUALS `Can I be compensated by my attorney` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `relieved of part` TRUE
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to compensate the principal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `no relief` FALSE EQUALS `Can I be compensated by my attorney` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `no relief` FALSE
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to compensate the principal` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no relief` TRUE EQUALS `Can I be compensated by my attorney` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no relief` TRUE

-- s 74: arguments liable, honest and reasonable.
#ASSERT `Could I be relieved of personal liability` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could I be relieved of personal liability` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Could I be relieved of personal liability` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 135 (with mirrors).
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty if I use the power dishonestly` FALSE)'s `penalty units` EQUALS 600
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty if I use the power dishonestly` TRUE)'s `penalty units` EQUALS 2400
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty if I use the power dishonestly` FALSE)'s `years of imprisonment` EQUALS (`What is the maximum penalty for dishonest dealing with my power` FALSE)'s `years of imprisonment`
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty if I use the power dishonestly` TRUE)'s `penalty units` EQUALS (`What is the maximum penalty for dishonest dealing with my power` TRUE)'s `penalty units`
